<title>USA: CBOT posts record volume in 1996, up 5.6 percent.</title>
<headline>CBOT posts record volume in 1996, up 5.6 percent.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total volume at the Chicago Board of Trade in 1996 rose 5.6 percent from 1995 levels amid strong gains in agricultural contracts.</p>
<p>The CBOT traded 222,438,505 futures and options contracts last year, up from 210,673,044 in 1995, the exchange reported.</p>
<p>Total agricultural futures and options volume at the Chicago Board of Trade surged 30.1 percent in 1996 over 1995, setting an all-time yearly volume record of 65,369,379 contracts, the CBOT said.</p>
<p>Futures volume in U.S. Treasury bonds, 10-year notes and five-year notes declined slightly in 1996 from 1995, the exchange reported.</p>
